3 . Reflex Routing Logic (RRL)

RRL is the autonomous middleware that decides when to Validate, Limbo, or Burn.
It functions as the nervous system of the network.

Key Functions

Weighted Reflex Matrices: multi-factor scoring of behavioral signals.

Adaptive Thresholds: adjust automatically to global averages and RBGA policy.

Ethical Gradient Descent: self-correction loop minimizing deviation from moral vector.

Behavioral Feedback Channels: API link to sensors, devices, or agentic models.

RRL exists both in software and in PCP hardware micro-instructions; it is the bridge between code, circuit, and cognition.

